diff --git a/features/destroy-task.feature b/features/destroy-task.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5b15383
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/destroy-task.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+Feature: Removing a task with its destroy control
+
+  Each rendered task carries a destroy control that removes that single task
+  from the list and persists the change. The control is reachable through the
+  item's view, independent of the edit and clear-completed paths.
+
+  @captain
+  Scenario: Clicking a task's destroy button removes the task
+    Given the app is open
+    And the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is not present
+    And the task "Walk the dog" is present
diff --git a/features/html-escaping.feature b/features/html-escaping.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5b36858
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/html-escaping.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+Feature: HTML escaping of task titles
+
+  A task title that contains HTML markup must render as escaped text so the
+  markup is not interpreted as live elements in the list. The view renders the
+  title through the escaping helper before inserting it into the DOM.
+
+  @captain
+  Scenario: A task title with HTML markup renders escaped
+    Given the app is open
+    And the task list contains "<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>"
+    Then the task "<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>" renders its title as escaped text
